WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
Speaker 1: Well, a criminal investigation has&nbsp;
been opened into Florida Republican Governor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:12.480
Ron DeSantis stunt wherein he paid to fly 50&nbsp;
migrants from Texas to the Massachusetts island&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.880
of Martha's Vineyard. And wow, how quickly this&nbsp;
is all developed. Think back to the beginning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:23.580
when we first found out that Ron DeSantis,&nbsp;
remember Ron DeSantis, governor of Florida,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:32.160
paid millions of dollars in taxpayer money to&nbsp;
fly migrants from Texas to Martha's Vineyard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:39.000
We thought, well, it's a very stupid and brazen&nbsp;
and tasteless political stunt, but that's as far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:46.980
as it goes, at least potentially. We then learned,&nbsp;
oh, you know, the migrants were lied to. They were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:53.640
promised things. They were promised that they were&nbsp;
being taken to Boston for expedited something or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.840
rather and help getting jobs and whatever else&nbsp;
the case may be. That's not true. You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.960
that's sort of like fraudulent human trafficking.&nbsp;
Maybe there's something criminal there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:11.040
And yesterday on the show, I had three or four&nbsp;
different commentaries from lawyers saying, yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:17.520
this actually does seem like it's a crime. These&nbsp;
were folks that were trafficked illegally by Ron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.840
DeSantis and those deputized by Ron DeSantis for&nbsp;
this stunt. So that where we left that yesterday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:29.100
was what next? Is there an investigation? What&nbsp;
happens next? And now, indeed, there is a criminal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:35.280
investigation that has been opened. The Miami&nbsp;
Herald reporting Texas sheriff will investigate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:44.220
Florida flying a Venezuelan migrants to Martha's&nbsp;
Vineyard. We have video, in fact, of Bexar County&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:50.820
Sheriff Javier Salazar, who explained what&nbsp;
his investigation is going to be and remember.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:57.780
DeSantis is in Florida, but he decided&nbsp;
to get involved with Texas. And that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:04.604
why the sheriff is from Texas, the location,&nbsp;
the source where these migrants came from.&nbsp;

00:02:04.604 --> 00:02:11.040
Speaker 2: When we are opening up a case with&nbsp;
an investigation with regard to the suspected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:19.500
activities involving the 48 migrants from&nbsp;
Venezuela, that as we understand it at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:26.220
the facts of the case at this point are that on&nbsp;
Wednesday, September 14th, here in Bear County,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:34.860
in the city of San Antonio, our understanding is&nbsp;
that a Venezuelan migrant was paid what we would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:40.500
call a bird dog fee to recruit approximately&nbsp;
50 migrants from the area around a migrant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.480
resource center on San Pedro here in San Antonio.
Speaker 1: You know, they talk about Democrats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:51.180
as the criminals. This is this is just&nbsp;
straight up criminality. If it's as alleged.&nbsp;

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:58.980
Speaker 2: As we understand it, 48 migrants&nbsp;
were lured. I will use the word lured under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:06.600
false pretenses into into staying at a hotel for&nbsp;
a couple of days. They were taken by airplane.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:12.420
At a certain point, they were shuttled to an&nbsp;
airplane where they were flown to Florida and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:17.340
eventually flown to Martha's Vineyard. Again under&nbsp;
false pretenses is the information that we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:22.440
that they were promised work, they were promised&nbsp;
the solution to several of their problems. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:28.980
were taken to Martha's Vineyard. From what? For&nbsp;
what we can gather for nothing for little more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:36.300
than a photo op video up. And then they were&nbsp;
unceremoniously stranded in Martha's Vineyard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:43.200
What infuriates me the most about this case is&nbsp;
that here we have 48 people that are already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:48.240
on on hard times. Right. They are here&nbsp;
legally in our country at that point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.200
They have every right to be where they are.
Speaker 1: Now, remember that that's this is an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.200 --> 00:04:00.420
important detail. The right has been just using&nbsp;
the blanket term illegal immigrants. These are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:05.400
folks, as I understand it, and as it seems like&nbsp;
the sheriff understands it as well. And we'll see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:13.440
if he even explains this. Who were in the process&nbsp;
of having asylum asylum claims reviewed. Meaning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:19.740
that at this particular point in time, these&nbsp;
were not individuals subject to deportation for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:23.460
